From cf45559b52d0398b983101c00911bfc9e531ad1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaron Shahrabani <EMAIL>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:31:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: vdec: drop parked capture buffers on capture
 STREAMOFF

A capture buffer that comes back from the firmware with
HFI_BUFFERFLAG_READONLY is still used as a reference frame. If userspace
queues it again before the firmware releases it,
venus_helper_vb2_buf_queue() parks it on inst->delayed_process, and the
delayed work submits it once the RELEASE_BUFFER_REFERENCE event arrives.

On capture STREAMOFF all capture buffers are returned to userspace, but
the parked ones stay linked on delayed_process. After the next STREAMON
(a seek), the first RELEASE event makes the delayed work submit such a
stale entry while userspace owns the buffer, and when userspace queues
it again it reaches the firmware twice. On MSM8916 (firmware
VIDEO.VE.1.8) every seek in a GStreamer playbin then stopped a few
frames later with "session error: event id:1004"
(HFI_ERR_SESSION_INVALID_SESSION_ID). An ftrace/kprobe trace showed
buffer 1 parked during preroll, submitted from delayed_process_buf_func()
105 ms after the seek, queued again by userspace 41 ms later, and the
session error 0.4 ms after that.

Unlink the parked buffers when capture is stopped. A buffer that is
still READONLY when it is queued again is parked again by buf_queue.

Fixes: af2c3834c8ca ("[media] media: venus: adding core part and helper functions")
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
---
Found while testing David Heidelberg's "media: venus: vdec: Start
capture after a seek that streams CAPTURE first" (posted 2026-09-28,
Message-Id <20260928-venus-vdec-eos-v1-2-6e9eb3ce9849@ixit.cz>), which is
what lets seeks reach this path on MSM8916 at all; this patch does not
depend on it and applies to v7.3-rc6. It may conflict trivially with
"media: venus: vdec: Clear streamon flags on streaming errors" (also
under review), which touches the same function.

Tested on a Samsung Galaxy Tab A 9.7 (SM-T550, MSM8916, VIDEO.VE.1.8)
with a msm8916-mainline 7.3-rc2 based kernel (vdec.c identical to
v7.3-rc6 plus the patch above and the fixup I sent in reply to it):
flushing seeks to 0 s and 10 s in a 1080p H.264 clip with GStreamer
playbin3 stop a few frames later with "session error: event id:1004"
without this patch, and play on (3/3 and 2/2) with it, with no firmware
errors. Seeking in Firefox (FFmpeg h264_v4l2m2m) also works.
Not tested: other HFI versions, and a plain mainline kernel.

The stale entries are also on the list if userspace frees the buffers
after STREAMOFF; I have not seen that go wrong, and unlinking on
STREAMOFF closes that window too.

This was developed with an AI assistant (see the Assisted-by tag); I
reviewed and tested it and take responsibility for it.

 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
index 6a43ea1..5d70012 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
@@ -1288,10 +1288,22 @@ static void vdec_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q)
 
 	mutex_lock(&inst->lock);
 
-	if (q->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE)
+	if (q->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE) {
+		struct venus_buffer *buf, *n;
+
 		ret = vdec_stop_capture(inst);
-	else
+
+		/*
+		 * Capture buffers parked until the firmware releases them are
+		 * handed back to userspace below. Unlink them, or the delayed
+		 * work submits them again after the next STREAMON, while
+		 * userspace owns them (and they are queued a second time).
+		 */
+		list_for_each_entry_safe(buf, n, &inst->delayed_process, ref_list)
+			list_del_init(&buf->ref_list);
+	} else {
 		ret = vdec_stop_output(inst);
+	}
 
 	venus_helper_buffers_done(inst, q->type, VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
 
